Before the Quest and Castle, improving AC is important and you 
are at the mercy of the RNG.  If you can't find a scroll of 
enchant armor or you can't find a magic marker, then you are 
stuck with the armor you can find.  Additionaly If you have 
scrolls and a magic marker but no armor beyond basic stuff, is it 
worth it to hold out for those boots of speed, or magical gloves?

Gather up pieces of armor... Only wearing a +0 orcish helm?  
Gather all the helms you can find.  Let a pet or an altar 
determine if they are cursed, try on all the ones that aren't, or 
just take 'em to a convenient shop and see what they're worth. 
Shopkeepers pay more for +Enchanted items.  You'll never know 
when you find some +3 piece off a Green-Elf or a hill orc. Use 
scrolls and markers on your robe, it will serve you well.

Monks will have a lower AC by default without a suit of armor. 
You'll need to make up for this your wits and magic. Greater 
healing is a good book to find, magic missiles, jumping (a very 
stylish monk spell), haste self, charm monster, sleep and others 
will help keep you out of trouble.

When do you know when you are ready?  If you can move freely 
about the main dungeons and deal with encounters without taking 
too many scrapes then you should be able to survive some major 
scrapes in the Quest and the Castle... Remember there is no magic 
number for HP AC etc... Strategy is just as important.  Focus on 
the most dangerous monster, look for opprotunities to used ranged 
attacks, stay behind cover and leave an escape route. I've yet to 
do the Monk quest, but I hear its one of the trickier quests, so 
maybe the castle would be a better first, but do bring 
reflection.  Don't have magic resistance yet?  It can be tough 
for a monk to get MR, so be very cautious of Liches and certain 
Nagas.  A good attack spell is important here, since monks can't 
throw daggers, darts might do the trick but I've never done much 
with them.  If you can get to the castle at a lower XP level, 11-
13, you wont see as many of the nastier monsters, hopefully no 
big Liches or disenchanters, but the Minotaurs and Dragons will 
still be epic adversaries.

Strategy is the key though, and take time to plan your moves and 
prepare yourself for the worst.

Good luck


